dense_results.text:
Useful pipeline metrics include:

- retrieval latency;
- generation latency;
- number of retrieved chunks;
- citation support rate;
- abstention rate;
- token usage;
- estimated model cost.

Metrics should use stable names and bounded label values. Raw user questions
should not be used as metric labels because they create high-cardinality data.

Pydantic models can be converted into dictionaries or JSON-compatible
representations. Serialization is useful when storing:

- document metadata;
- chunk records;
- retrieval traces;
- evaluation results;
- API responses.

A serialized object should preserve stable identifiers such as `document_id`,
`chunk_id`, and `corpus_version`.

